{
  "dom_id": "step-q96841",
  "name": "Question 12",
  "problem": "Given $X∼U\\{8,9,10,…,34\\},$ compute $P(12\\le X\\le 25).$",
  "worked_solution": "If $X$ follows a discrete uniform distribution over a set $S,$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{|S|}, & x\\in S \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $X∼U\\{8,9,10,…,34\\},$ and the set $S=\\{8,9,10,…,34\\}$ has $|S|=34-8+1=27$ items. So, we have\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{27}, & x=8,9,10,…,34 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn $S,$ the items that satisfy $12\\le X\\le 25$ are $12,13,14,…,25.$ There are $25-12+1=14$ of these items. Therefore,\n\n$$\nP(12\\le X\\le 25)=14\\cdot \\frac{1}{27}=\\frac{14}{27}.\n$$",
